00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.960
episode

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.960
"A Lilac

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.960
 Blooming in the Barracks"

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.890
Brother! Here, I've washed your
shirts and undergarments.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.490
Thanks.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.860
Here's the next batch.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.100
Could you take care of it before
the next visitor's day?

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.360
Sure.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:52.570
This is a lot!

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:57.670
Sorry, things are really busy right now,
so I don't have time to wash them myself.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:58.870
I know you are.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:02:59.890
Well then...

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.240
I got paid.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.380
Thank you.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.780
How is mom's illness?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.340
Same as always.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.500
I see...

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.880
Hey, she's here!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.040
Diane is here!

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.250
Are you serious?!

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:13.790
Oh, that's right!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:15.220
Today's visitor's day!

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.170
She's always so cute!

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:25.390
How could such a thickset guy like
him have such a cute little sister?

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.730
If I get married, it's going to
be with someone like her.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.440
Maybe I'll ask her out on
a date on my next day off.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.410
You idiot!

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.280
Alain will kill you if you do!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.370
Bet he will, too.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.720
This is our new commander.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.390
Thank you for looking after my brother.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.380
I'm Alain's sister, Diane.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.070
Your brother has been helpful to me, as well.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.350
I'm Oscar François.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.940
General Bouillé...!

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:23.030
Please forgive me for my actions the other day.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.360
Don't worry about what happened.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.560
Your father and I are old friends.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.740
I'm not the least bit offended.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:31.800
You're too kind.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.210
More importantly, I've come here today
to assign you a special mission.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.140
I'm sure you're already aware,

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:41.170
but Duke Ardelos and his family are
currently visiting our country from Spain.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:45.130
Yes, I hear they are here to promote their
country's goodwill with our royal family.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.980
We've been informed the
terrorists are targeting them.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.680
They are plotting to attack Duke Ardelos and
undermine the authority of our royal family.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.690
To further complicate matters,
the family is planning to travel the provinces.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.560
That's where you come in.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.790
I want you and your company to guard them.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:04.030
Your Excellency, with all due respect,
I am no longer in the Royal Guards.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.230
I'm aware of that.

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.500
You're implying this is a mission
for the Royal Guards, aren't you?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.970
However, the Royal Guards have
their hands full right now.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:15.870
Also, no one in the other units knows
how to treat foreign royals properly.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.100
That's why I'm specifically asking you to do it.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.090
We depart early tomorrow morning.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.930
We'll guard them from a distance to avoid intruding
on the family's visit as much as possible.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.690
Depending on the situation,
we may make camp outdoors.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.350
Everyone should be equipped
for an expedition.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.730
Where's your gun?

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.460
Why aren't you in line with your musket?

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.570
I lost it.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.150
Where? When?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.140
I-I don't know.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:47.360
I can't remember when or where I lost it.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.370
What?!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.750
Do you really think you can get away with such an ambiguous answer after losing your valuable musket?!

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:58.070
A soldier who loses the gun handed to him by his
country without proper reason, could be subjected...

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:00.000
...to corporal punishment or
worse case, be imprisoned!

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.320
Try and remember.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.070
Remember where and when you lost it!

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:03.920
Right now!

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:04.960
Fine with me.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.790
Corporal punishment, imprisonment, whatever...

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:07.430
It's fine.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.180
What's your name?

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:11.770
Lazare Dressel.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.530
Colonel d'Agout.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.190
Yes!

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:18.500
Go to the armory and have them
release another gun for Lazare.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.140
Make up some kind of excuse.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:21.370
Understood!

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:45.390
That's Duke Ardelos' procession.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.510
We'll split up into two units from here.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.670
The first unit will guard Duke Ardelos.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:53.740
The other unit will be a flying column, positioned
in the front and rear of the procession.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.970
Its objective is to discover
the terrorists by any means.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.180
Colonel d'Agout.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.040
Yes!

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.110
You command the guard unit.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.880
I'll lead the flying column.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.400
Please be careful.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.420
This is Ardelos of the Kingdom of Spain.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.540
And this is his wife and daughter.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.740
We'll kill the entire family.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.300
That way, it'll be more shocking.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.380
The larger the shock, the more
\hfrightful the nobles will become.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:37.920
That's when we move.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:42.310
Monsieur Robespierre's vision of creating
a National Assembly is one way,

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.690
but that'll take too long.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.660
That's unacceptable to me.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.320
Ardelos' procession has left Versailles
and is heading north.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.730
All right. Comrades!

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:52.280
Let's go!

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.170
Hold on, Saint-Just.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.400
Today isn't a good day.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.240
The French Guards are tightly guarding him.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.300
Nothing to worry.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.210
We also have a comrade in the French Guards.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.460
Alain, André.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.790
We'll search that château.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:19.490
Follow me!

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:20.140
Yes!

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:20.140
Yes!

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:23.060
The rest of you, wait here until I give the signal.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:23.890
Yes!

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.890
We'll attack Ardelos in the village of Hallencourt.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.920
I instructed our comrade in the French Guards,

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.950
to kill the commander before
the procession arrives there.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.870
Hey, where are you going?

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.310
She ordered us to stay here!

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.280
Yeah, there's something I need
to tell the commander.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:10.710
André! How is it?!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.570
All clear!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:15.490
All clear on my end, as well!

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:16.780
All right, good.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:17.980
Check the cellar then!

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:19.780
I'll check the upper floors!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:20.280
Yes!

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:21.010
Okay!

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.800
I said one person is enough
to check the upper floors!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:44.410
What...?! What are you doing here?

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:48.110
Did you forget my order to wait in the forest?

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:48.850
Go back immediately!

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.650
Don't be so upright, Commander.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.570
I came to help you.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.150
Go back.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.280
If you defy my order, I can have
you tried by court-martial.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:23.810
If you die, the French Guards won't be
able to focus on guarding Duke Ardelos!

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:27.590
You're with the terrorists?!

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:30.560
So long, kind woman commander!

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.600
What was that gun shot just now?!

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:50.340
Oscar!

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.800
Who's your leader?

00:10:57.620 --> 00:11:01.550
If you say his name, I can grant you
some leniency in your punishment.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.830
Give it up!

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.480
You won't be able to kill me with just one arm!

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:18.440
You should worry about treating
your wound instead.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.080
At this rate, you'll die before you can kill me!

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:25.910
He told me to kill you no matter what!

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.080
It's for the sake of the new era...

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.500
I don't care what happens to me!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.390
Don't shoot!

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.490
It seems he failed.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:14.250
What now?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.330
''What now,'' you say?

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.960
We don't make plans just to change them later.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.130
We carry them out regardless!

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:32.110
Commander!

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.380
You have a message from Colonel d'Agout!

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:40.940
Duke Ardelos' procession has arrived safely at
tonight's lodging in the village of Hallencourt!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.500
Colonel d'Agout will secure
the inside of the village.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:55.000
We'll secure the outer areas
and the entryways to the village.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.540
Meal Team, find a campsite where we
can also keep an eye on the village!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.250
Yes!

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.920
Boy, I'm sleepy...

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:21.130
Hey, André.

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.690
Give her up. It's for the better.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.700
Commanding the company,
delegating orders efficiently...

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.120
She's quite good at what she does.

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:33.080
But to me it looks as though she's desperately
trying to run away from something.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.540
That's why she doesn't know to loosen up.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:41.510
Falling in love with a woman like
that is just asking for trouble.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:45.850
The man will become just another casualty
and won't have enough lives to spare.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:46.880
Here.

00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:58.560
Here.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.030
Thanks.

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:11.030
So you're willing to abandon
your life for that woman, huh?

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:15.740
Just because you're going blind,
doesn't mean you should become reckless.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.150
It's pretty bad, isn't it?

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:22.450
We live in close proximity, so even I can tell.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.960
Does that woman know about your eyes?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:26.670
No.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.430
Alain, don't tell anyone about this... Please!

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:31.140
Sure.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.330
What the...?!

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:32.420
Everyone, keep calm!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.700
Keep your positions!

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:36.190
Put the fire out!

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.260
Don't let the fire spread to the building!

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.660
Put the fire out!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.200
Colonel!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.380
Where's Duke Ardelos?!

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.090
He's in his room!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.590
Is Duke Ardelos unharmed?!

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:56.510
Damn it!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.200
Hey, André!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:17.910
That's...!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:29.840
Oscar!

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:31.710
André!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.520
How many are after us?!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.430
There are three of them!

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.590
Three, eh?

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:45.230
All right, take them on and kill them!

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:46.900
I'll head back to Paris!

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:47.590
Got it!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.680
Go get her, André...!

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:38.370
One, two...

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:39.890
One, two...

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:42.440
One, two...

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:53.190
It's regrettable the terrorists got away,

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:56.780
but thanks to you, Duke Ardelos and his
procession were able to return home safely.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:00.130
You've done an excellent job on this mission.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:00.820
Thank you.

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:05.800
By the way, there's something
I wish to show you.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:06.600
Show her.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.290
Yes!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:20.650
This is...!

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:24.930
It was being sold at a pawnshop
when the Military Police found it.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:29.160
We learned it was issued to
Company B from the serial number.

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:33.430
Find out whom it belongs to and report
it to the Military Police promptly.

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:36.130
If the soldier sold it, it's an act of treason.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:37.480
He'll be executed by firing squad.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:52.960
<i>Where is your gun? Why aren't
you in line with your musket?</i>

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:55.670
<i>I lost it.</i>

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:17.910
Military Police!

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.610
Is there a man named Lazare Dressel here?!

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.570
Th-That's me...

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:35.890
Come in.

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:41.470
What are you both doing here?

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.680
Could you answer a question for me?

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.480
What's with the formalities all of the sudden?

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.140
Just what if...

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.440
What would you do if André here, says
he wants to marry my little sister?

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:53.190
Hey, Alain!

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.480
Shut up!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:55.500
You be quiet!

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:58.110
Answer me, Commander.

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.720
I don't know what you're talking about,

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.110
but if that's how André feels and
wishes to do, he's free to do so.

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:06.560
I figured that's what you'd say.

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:10.890
Hey, André, she doesn't know a thing about you.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:14.080
There's no need for you to stand up for her.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:20.000
Still, Alain, it's unthinkable to me
that Oscar would do such a thing!

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:23.970
I want you outside, Commander!

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.440
What is this about?!

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:27.140
If there's something you wish
to say, say it outright!

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:30.110
Lazare was taken away!

00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:31.100
By the Military Police!

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:32.080
What?!

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:35.450
Selling your men out, eh?
You sure are something, Commander!

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:36.270
I—!

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:40.020
I said, come outside!

00:21:43.390 --> 00:21:44.490
Damn you!

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:49.500
I'm disappointed in you.

00:21:49.500 --> 00:21:51.710
I was just starting to have a
better opinion of you, too.

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:56.670
Believe me, I've done no such thing as
selling Lazare to the Military Police!

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:57.730
Believe you?

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:59.290
You really expect me to believe you?!

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:01.150
Lazare will be executed by firing squad!

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:02.680
No matter how it turns out, I can't forgive you!

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:06.920
I heard your weapon of choice is a sword.

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:08.130
Fine with me! Draw your sword!

